content:
# Comprehensive Code Audit Report — Agent 10

**Audited Files:**
1. `new/client/src/pages/ManageData.jsx`
2. `new/client/src/pages/UserManagement.jsx`
3. `new/client/src/pages/Settings.jsx`
4. `new/client/src/pages/CarbonIntensity.jsx`
5. `new/client/src/pages/DashboardEnhanced.jsx`

---

## 1. new/client/src/pages/ManageData.jsx

### [BUG MD-01] React State Management: Memory Leak & Unmounted Component Updates in Initial Data Load
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/ManageData.jsx`, Lines 653–665
- **Category:** React State Management / Memory Leak
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  // Fetch Data on Load
  useEffect(() => {
      fetchFacilities();
      fetchCustomFactors();
      fetchProduction();
      fetchSources();
      fetchMitigations();
      fetchCbamExports();
      fetchOgmpSurveys();
      fetchGoals();
      fetchBaseYears();
      fetchPendingEmissions();
      fetchSbti();
  }, []);
  ```
- **Explanation:**
  Eleven asynchronous network requests are initiated in parallel when the component mounts. None of these fetch functions (`fetchFacilities`, `fetchCustomFactors`, etc.) check whether the component is still mounted when their promises resolve. If the user navigates to another page (e.g. Dashboard or Settings) before all requests complete, multiple `setState` calls (`setFacilities`, `setCustomFactors`, `setProductionData`, etc.) are triggered on an unmounted component, causing React memory leak warnings and unnecessary work.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  useEffect(() => {
      let isMounted = true;
      const loadAll = async () => {
          try {
              if (isMounted) {
                  fetchFacilities();
                  fetchCustomFactors();
                  fetchProduction();
                  fetchSources();
                  fetchMitigations();
                  fetchCbamExports();
                  fetchOgmpSurveys();
                  fetchGoals();
                  fetchBaseYears();
                  fetchPendingEmissions();
                  fetchSbti();
              }
          } catch (e) {
              console.error("Error during initial data fetch:", e);
          }
      };
      loadAll();
      return () => {
          isMounted = false;
      };
  }, []);
  ```

---

### [BUG MD-02] UI Rendering & Layout: Table Column Misalignment (`colSpan="8"` vs 11 Header Columns)
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/ManageData.jsx`, Lines 2748–2802
- **Category:** UI Rendering / Table Layout Bug
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```jsx
  2749: <thead>
  2750:     <tr>
  2751:         <th>Activity</th>
  2752:         <th>Division</th>
  2753:         <th>Region</th>
  2754:         <th>Year</th>
  2755:         <th>Month</th>
  2756:         <th style={{ textAlign: 'right' }}>Oil (bbl)</th>
  2757:         <th style={{ textAlign: 'right' }}>Gas (mcf)</th>
  2758:         <th style={{ textAlign: 'right' }}>Gross Gas (MMSm³)</th>
  2759:         <th style={{ textAlign: 'right' }}>Total (MMBOE)</th>
  2760:         <th style={{ textAlign: 'right' }}>Saleable (MMBOE)</th>
  2761:         <th style={{ textAlign: 'center' }}>Actions</th>
  2762:     </tr>
  2763: </thead>
  ...
  2794: {filteredProduction.length === 0 && (
  2795:     <tr>
  2796:         <td colSpan="8" style={{ textAlign: 'center', padding: '40px', color: 'var(--text-secondary)' }}>
  2797:             No production records found.
  2798:         </td>
  2799:     </tr>
  2800: )}
  ```
- **Explanation:**
  The `<thead>` of the Annual Production Records table defines **11 columns**. When `filteredProduction` is empty (e.g. no records or filter mismatch), the empty-state `<td>` hardcodes `colSpan="8"`. This leaves 3 columns unspanned, causing the empty table cell to truncate prematurely, misaligning borders and headers across the table container.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```jsx
  {filteredProduction.length === 0 && (
      <tr>
          <td colSpan="11" style={{ textAlign: 'center', padding: '40px', color: 'var(--text-secondary)' }}>
              No production records found.
          </td>
      </tr>
  )}
  ```

---

### [BUG MD-03] UI Rendering / Filter: Inconsistent Facility ID Access (`d.facilityId` vs `d.facility_id`)
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/ManageData.jsx`, Lines 1315–1317 & Line 2771
- **Category:** Undefined Property Access / Filter Bug
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  1315: const getFilteredProduction = () => productionData.filter(d => {
  1316:     const fac = facilities.find(f => f.id === d.facilityId);
  1317:     const facName = fac ? fac.name.toLowerCase() : String(d.facilityId).toLowerCase();
  ...
  2771:     const fac = facilities.find(f => f.id === d.facilityId);
  ```
- **Explanation:**
  In `productionData`, records can contain either `facility_id` (standard snake_case used by DB and POST form) or `facilityId` (camelCase returned by the GET route). If `d.facilityId` is undefined, `facilities.find(f => f.id === undefined)` fails to find the facility, and `String(d.facilityId)` produces the string `"undefined"`. As a result, searching for a facility name fails, filtering by division/activity fails to correlate, and the table displays `"undefined"`.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  const getFilteredProduction = () => productionData.filter(d => {
      const fid = d.facility_id ?? d.facilityId;
      const fac = facilities.find(f => String(f.id) === String(fid));
      const facName = fac ? fac.name.toLowerCase() : String(fid || '').toLowerCase();
      const matchesSearch = facName.includes(searchTerm.toLowerCase()) || d.year.toString().includes(searchTerm) || (d.activity?.toLowerCase() || '').includes(searchTerm.toLowerCase());
      const matchesAct = filterActivity ? (matchesActivity(d.activity, filterActivity) || (fac && matchesActivity(fac.activity, filterActivity))) : true;
      const matchesDiv = filterDivision ? (d.division === filterDivision || (fac && fac.division === filterDivision)) : true;
      const matchesReg = matchesRegionCheck(fac, filterRegion);
      const matchesYear = filterYear ? d.year.toString() === filterYear.toString() : true;
      return matchesSearch && matchesAct && matchesDiv && matchesReg && matchesYear;
  });
  ```

---

### [BUG MD-04] Form Handling & Validation: Empty String Values Sent to Float Backend Columns
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/ManageData.jsx`, Lines 573–577 & Lines 920–934
- **Category:** Form Validation / Backend Payload Structure
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  573: const [facilityForm, setFacilityForm] = useState({
  574:     name: '', activity: '', division: '', field: '', location: '',
  575:     boundary_type: '', boundary_detail: '', equity_share_pct: '',
  576:     segment: '', latitude: '', longitude: ''
  577: });
  ...
  930: await api.post('/facilities', {
  931:     ...facilityForm,
  932:     boundary_notes: fullBoundary // Map back to API field
  933: });
  ```
- **Explanation:**
  `latitude`, `longitude`, and `equity_share_pct` are initialized as empty strings `""`. If the user submits the form leaving coordinates or equity share blank, the payload contains `""`. In SQLAlchemy/PostgreSQL/SQLite, inserting `""` into `db.Column(db.Float)` raises a database `DataError: invalid input syntax for type double precision` or fails float conversion, returning a 500 error.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  const handleAddFacility = async () => {
      if (!facilityForm.name?.trim() || !facilityForm.activity || !facilityForm.division) {
          return toast.error('Name, Activity, and Division are required');
      }
      try {
          const fullBoundary = facilityForm.boundary_detail
              ? `${facilityForm.boundary_type} - ${facilityForm.boundary_detail}`
              : facilityForm.boundary_type;

          const payload = {
              ...facilityForm,
              name: facilityForm.name.trim(),
              boundary_notes: fullBoundary,
              equity_share_pct: facilityForm.equity_share_pct !== '' ? parseFloat(facilityForm.equity_share_pct) : 100.0,
              latitude: facilityForm.latitude !== '' ? parseFloat(facilityForm.latitude) : null,
              longitude: facilityForm.longitude !== '' ? parseFloat(facilityForm.longitude) : null,
          };

          await api.post('/facilities', payload);
          toast.success('Region added!');
          setFacilityForm({
              name: '', activity: '', division: '', field: '', location: '',
              boundary_type: '', boundary_detail: '', equity_share_pct: '',
              segment: '', latitude: '', longitude: ''
          });
          fetchFacilities();
      } catch (err) { 
          toast.error(err?.response?.data?.error || 'Failed to add region'); 
      }
  };
  ```

---

### [BUG MD-05] UI Rendering & Edge Cases: `NaN` Rendered in Base Year Recalculation History Table
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/ManageData.jsx`, Lines 3210–3213 & Lines 3243–3248
- **Category:** UI Edge Cases / Arithmetic Bug
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  3210: const diff = (b.adjusted_emissions !== null && b.previous_emissions !== null && b.adjusted_emissions !== undefined && b.previous_emissions !== undefined)
  3211:     ? b.adjusted_emissions - b.previous_emissions
  3212:     : null;
  ...
  3243: {diff !== null ? (
  3244:     <span style={{ color: diff > 0 ? '#b91c1c' : diff < 0 ? '#15803d' : 'var(--text-secondary)', fontWeight: 600 }}>
  3245:         {diff > 0 ? `+${diff.toLocaleString()}` : diff.toLocaleString()} tCO₂e
  3246:     </span>
  3247: ) : '-'}
  ```
- **Explanation:**
  If either `b.adjusted_emissions` or `b.previous_emissions` is non-numeric (e.g. stored as an invalid string), `b.adjusted_emissions - b.previous_emissions` evaluates to `NaN`. Because in JS `NaN !== null` evaluates to `true`, and both `NaN > 0` and `NaN < 0` are `false`, it evaluates `diff.toLocaleString()`, rendering `"NaN tCO₂e"` in the table cell.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  const adj = b.adjusted_emissions != null ? Number(b.adjusted_emissions) : null;
  const prev = b.previous_emissions != null ? Number(b.previous_emissions) : null;
  const diff = (adj != null && prev != null && !isNaN(adj) && !isNaN(prev)) ? adj - prev : null;
  ```
  ```jsx
  <td style={{ textAlign: 'right', fontSize: '0.88rem' }}>
      {diff !== null && isFinite(diff) ? (
          <span style={{ color: diff > 0 ? '#b91c1c' : diff < 0 ? '#15803d' : 'var(--text-secondary)', fontWeight: 600 }}>
              {diff > 0 ? `+${diff.toLocaleString()}` : diff.toLocaleString()} tCO₂e
          </span>
      ) : '-'}
  </td>
  ```

---

### [BUG MD-06] Form Handling: Unchecked `NaN` Passed to `JSON.stringify` on Goal & Base Year Submissions
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/ManageData.jsx`, Lines 820–828 & Lines 868–878
- **Category:** Form Validation / Payload Structure
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  825: await api.post('/goals', {
  826:     year: parseInt(goalForm.year),
  827:     target_amount: parseFloat(goalForm.target_amount)
  828: });
  ```
- **Explanation:**
  If user inputs `"abc"` into `goalForm.target_amount`, `parseFloat("abc")` returns `NaN`. `JSON.stringify({ target_amount: NaN })` serializes `NaN` to `null`. The backend receives `{ year: 2024, target_amount: null }`, bypassing client validation and triggering a 400/500 error from the server.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  const handleSaveGoal = async () => {
      const year = parseInt(goalForm.year, 10);
      const target = parseFloat(goalForm.target_amount);
      if (isNaN(year) || isNaN(target) || target < 0) {
          return toast.error('A valid target year and non-negative target emission amount (tCO₂e) are required');
      }
      try {
          await api.post('/goals', { year, target_amount: target });
          toast.success(editingGoalYear ? 'Emission goal updated!' : 'Emission goal saved!');
          setEditingGoalYear(null);
          setGoalForm({ year: new Date().getFullYear(), target_amount: '' });
          fetchGoals();
      } catch (err) {
          toast.error(err.response?.data?.error || 'Failed to save emission goal');
      }
  };
  ```

---

### [BUG MD-07] UI Rendering & Modal State: Conversion Modal State Leak on Cancel
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/ManageData.jsx`, Lines 1215–1243 & Line 4142
- **Category:** Modal State Leak
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```jsx
  4140: <Modal
  4141:     isOpen={convertModal.isOpen}
  4142:     onClose={() => setConvertModal(prev => ({ ...prev, isOpen: false }))}
  4143:     title={`Convert Volume (${convertModal.type === 'gas' ? 'Gas: m³ → mscf' : 'Oil: m³ → bbl'})`}
  4144: >
  ```
- **Explanation:**
  When the user closes the conversion modal via the close icon or backdrop (`onClose`), `prev.value` is retained. If reopened later for another production field (e.g. switching from Gas to Oil), the previous input is leaked into the input field.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```jsx
  <Modal
      isOpen={convertModal.isOpen}
      onClose={() => setConvertModal({ isOpen: false, type: 'gas', value: '' })}
      title={`Convert Volume (${convertModal.type === 'gas' ? 'Gas: m³ → mscf' : 'Oil: m³ → bbl'})`}
  >
  ```

---

## 2. new/client/src/pages/UserManagement.jsx

### [BUG UM-01] CRITICAL RUNTIME CRASH: `TypeError: S.roleBadge is not a function`
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/UserManagement.jsx`, Lines 1588–1598
- **Category:** Undefined Property Access / Fatal Runtime Error
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```jsx
  1588: {resetTarget.role && (
  1589:   <span
  1590:     style={S.roleBadge(
  1591:       getRoleMeta(resetTarget.role).color,
  1592:       getRoleMeta(resetTarget.role).bg,
  1593:       getRoleMeta(resetTarget.role).border,
  1594:     )}
  1595:   >
  1596:     {getRoleMeta(resetTarget.role).label}
  1597:   </span>
  1598: )}
  ```
- **Explanation:**
  In the Reset Password slide-over Drawer, line 1590 calls `S.roleBadge(...)`. However, in the style helper object `S` (lines 84–399), `roleBadge` does NOT exist. Instead, line 258 defines `regionPill: (color, bg, border) => ({ ... })` with the exact same three arguments.
  Whenever an IT Admin or IT Manager clicks the "Modify / Reset Password" key button on any user row, `setResetTarget(u)` causes the drawer to render, which immediately throws:
  **`TypeError: S.roleBadge is not a function`**.
  This crashes the React component tree with a fatal error.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```jsx
  {resetTarget.role && (
    <span
      style={S.regionPill(
        getRoleMeta(resetTarget.role).color,
        getRoleMeta(resetTarget.role).bg,
        getRoleMeta(resetTarget.role).border,
      )}
    >
      {getRoleMeta(resetTarget.role).label}
    </span>
  )}
  ```

---

### [BUG UM-02] React State Management: Memory Leak via Uncleaned `setTimeout` in `handleSubmit`
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/UserManagement.jsx`, Line 616
- **Category:** Memory Leak / Unmounted Component State Update
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  612: setIsModalOpen(false);
  ...
  616: setTimeout(() => fetchData(true, true), 800);
  ```
- **Explanation:**
  When a user is created or updated, `setTimeout(() => fetchData(true, true), 800)` is scheduled. If the user navigates to another page within 800ms of submitting, the timer fires and triggers `fetchData`, which invokes `setUsers`, `setRegions`, and `setLoading` on an unmounted component. No timer reference is held or cleared on component unmount.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  // At component top level:
  const syncTimerRef = useRef(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    return () => {
      if (syncTimerRef.current) clearTimeout(syncTimerRef.current);
    };
  }, []);

  // Inside handleSubmit:
  setIsModalOpen(false);
  syncTimerRef.current = setTimeout(() => {
    fetchData(true, true);
  }, 800);
  ```

---

### [BUG UM-03] React State Management: Missing Unmount Guard and Request Race Condition in `fetchData`
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/UserManagement.jsx`, Lines 439–473
- **Category:** Async Race Condition / Unmounted Component Update
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  const fetchData = async (silent = false, keepOptimistic = false) => {
    if (!silent) setLoading(true);
    try {
      const usersRes = await api.get("/auth/users");
      const serverUsers = usersRes.data;
      ...
      setUsers(serverUsers);
    } catch {
      if (!silent) toast.error("Failed to load users");
    }
  ```
- **Explanation:**
  `fetchData` executes independent asynchronous API requests without checking if the component is mounted when promises settle. If an unauthorized state change or fast navigation occurs, `setUsers` and `setRegions` will execute against an unmounted component.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  const isMountedRef = useRef(true);
  useEffect(() => {
    isMountedRef.current = true;
    return () => {
      isMountedRef.current = false;
    };
  }, []);

  const fetchData = async (silent = false, keepOptimistic = false) => {
    if (!silent && isMountedRef.current) setLoading(true);
    try {
      const usersRes = await api.get("/auth/users");
      if (!isMountedRef.current) return;
      const serverUsers = usersRes.data;
      if (keepOptimistic) {
        const serverIds = new Set(serverUsers.map((u) => u.id));
        setUsers((prev) => {
          const optimistic = prev.filter((u) => !serverIds.has(u.id));
          return [...serverUsers, ...optimistic];
        });
      } else {
        setUsers(serverUsers);
      }
    } catch {
      if (!silent && isMountedRef.current) toast.error("Failed to load users");
    }

    try {
      const regionsRes = await api.get("/facilities/all-regions");
      if (!isMountedRef.current) return;
      setRegions(Array.isArray(regionsRes.data) ? regionsRes.data : []);
    } catch {
      if (isMountedRef.current) setRegions([]);
      if (!silent && isMountedRef.current) toast.error("Failed to load facility regions");
    }

    if (!silent && isMountedRef.current) setLoading(false);
  };
  ```

---

### [BUG UM-04] UI Rendering / Filter: Regional Filter Leakage
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/UserManagement.jsx`, Lines 734–748
- **Category:** Filter Bug
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  734: const filteredUsers = users.filter((u) => {
  735:   const byRegion =
  736:     !filterRegion ||
  737:     u.location === filterRegion ||
  738:     u.role === "admin" ||
  739:     u.role === "it_admin" ||
  740:     u.role === "it_manager" ||
  741:     u.role === "it";
  742:   const byRole =
  743:     !filterRole ||
  744:     u.role === filterRole ||
  745:     (filterRole === "it_manager" && ["it_admin", "it_manager"].includes(u.role)) ||
  746:     (filterRole === "it_admin" && ["it_admin", "it_manager"].includes(u.role));
  747:   return byRegion && byRole;
  748: });
  ```
- **Explanation:**
  When an IT manager filters users by a specific Region (e.g. "Laghouat"), the condition `u.role === "admin" || u.role === "it_admin" || u.role === "it_manager" || u.role === "it"` forces all global admins and IT personnel to appear in the table regardless of region. This prevents the administrator from viewing strictly regional personnel for auditing.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  const filteredUsers = users.filter((u) => {
    const byRegion = !filterRegion || u.location === filterRegion;
    const byRole =
      !filterRole ||
      u.role === filterRole ||
      (["it_admin", "it_manager"].includes(filterRole) && ["it_admin", "it_manager"].includes(u.role));
    return byRegion && byRole;
  });
  ```

---

### [BUG UM-05] UI Rendering / Statistics: Super User (`superuser`) Count Missing from Stats Grid
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/UserManagement.jsx`, Lines 728–732 & Lines 842–900
- **Category:** UI Logic / Incomplete Statistics
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  728: const totalUsers = users.length;
  729: const adminCount = users.filter((u) => u.role === "admin").length;
  730: const itAdminCount = users.filter((u) => ["it_admin", "it_manager"].includes(u.role)).length;
  731: const itCount = users.filter((u) => u.role === "it").length;
  732: const standardCount = users.filter((u) => u.role === "user").length;
  ```
- **Explanation:**
  The breakdown of user counts accounts for `admin`, `it_admin`/`it_manager`, `it`, and `user`. However, `superuser` (Regional Managers) is not counted in any category. Consequently, `standardCount + adminCount + itAdminCount + itCount` does not equal `totalUsers`, creating a discrepancy on the header KPI tiles.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  const totalUsers = users.length;
  const adminCount = users.filter((u) => u.role === "admin").length;
  const superuserCount = users.filter((u) => u.role === "superuser").length;
  const itAdminCount = users.filter((u) => ["it_admin", "it_manager"].includes(u.role)).length;
  const itCount = users.filter((u) => u.role === "it").length;
  const standardCount = users.filter((u) => u.role === "user").length;
  ```
  Add a stat card for `Super Users` in the stat row:
  ```javascript
  {
    label: "Super Users",
    value: superuserCount,
    icon: <Shield size={20} />,
    color: "#8b5cf6",
    bg: "#f3e8ff",
  }
  ```

---

## 3. new/client/src/pages/Settings.jsx

### [BUG ST-01] React State Management: Unmounted Component State Updates in `loadSettings`
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/Settings.jsx`, Lines 96–162
- **Category:** React State Management / Memory Leak
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  useEffect(() => {
    loadSettings();
  }, []);

  const loadSettings = async () => {
    try {
      setLoading(true);
      const [settingsRes, facRes] = await Promise.all([
        api.get("/auth/settings").catch(() => ({ data: {} })),
        api.get("/facilities").catch(() => ({ data: [] })),
      ]);
      const settings = settingsRes.data;
      if (settings) {
        if (settings.gwp_standard) setGwpStandard(settings.gwp_standard);
        ...
  ```
- **Explanation:**
  If the user quickly leaves the Settings page, the unresolved `Promise.all` completes after unmount and invokes over 12 state setters (`setGwpStandard`, `setDefaultBaseYear`, `setGlobalThreshold`, `setUpstreamTarget`, `setMidstreamTarget`, `setCopernicusUsername`, `setCopernicusPassword`, etc.) and `setLoading(false)`.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  useEffect(() => {
    let isMounted = true;
    const loadSettings = async () => {
      try {
        setLoading(true);
        const [settingsRes, facRes] = await Promise.all([
          api.get("/auth/settings").catch(() => ({ data: {} })),
          api.get("/facilities").catch(() => ({ data: [] })),
        ]);
        if (!isMounted) return;

        const settings = settingsRes.data;
        if (settings) {
          if (settings.gwp_standard) setGwpStandard(settings.gwp_standard);
          if (settings.ogmp_default_base_year) setDefaultBaseYear(settings.ogmp_default_base_year);
          if (settings.reconciliation_threshold) setGlobalThreshold(settings.reconciliation_threshold);
          if (settings.ogmp_upstream_target_pct !== undefined) setUpstreamTarget(Number(settings.ogmp_upstream_target_pct));
          if (settings.ogmp_midstream_target_pct !== undefined) setMidstreamTarget(Number(settings.ogmp_midstream_target_pct));
          if (settings.copernicus_username) setCopernicusUsername(settings.copernicus_username);
          if (settings.copernicus_password) setCopernicusPassword(settings.copernicus_password);
          if (settings.copernicus_client_id) {
            setCopernicusClientId(settings.copernicus_client_id);
            setAuthMode("oauth_client");
          }
          if (settings.copernicus_client_secret) setCopernicusClientSecret(settings.copernicus_client_secret);
          if (settings.copernicus_qa_threshold !== undefined) setCopernicusQaThreshold(Number(settings.copernicus_qa_threshold));
          if (settings.copernicus_enabled !== undefined) setCopernicusEnabled(Boolean(settings.copernicus_enabled));
          if (settings.unit_system) setUnitSystem(settings.unit_system);
          if (settings.auto_flag_discrepancy !== undefined) setAutoFlagDiscrepancy(settings.auto_flag_discrepancy);
        }

        const facList = facRes.data;
        if (facList && Array.isArray(facList)) {
          setFacilities(facList);
          const initialMap = {};
          facList.forEach((f) => {
            initialMap[f.id] = {
              operator_status: f.operator_status || "operated",
              country: f.country || "Algeria",
              ogmp_membership_year: f.ogmp_membership_year || 2023,
              reconciliation_threshold: f.reconciliation_threshold || 20.0,
            };
          });
          setFacilityEdits(initialMap);
        }
      } catch (err) {
        console.error("Failed to load settings:", err);
        if (isMounted) toast.error("Failed to load settings");
      } finally {
        if (isMounted) setLoading(false);
      }
    };
    loadSettings();
    return () => {
      isMounted = false;
    };
  }, []);
  ```

---

### [BUG ST-02] UI Rendering & Edge Cases: `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'operator_status')`
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/Settings.jsx`, Line 287
