### [BUG DE-01] UI Rendering & Arithmetic: Division by Zero in Linear Regression Forecasting
- **Location:** `new/client/src/pages/DashboardEnhanced.jsx`, Lines 49–59
- **Category:** Zero Division / NaN Rendering Bug
- **Code Snippet:**
  ```javascript
  49: const slope = (n * sumXY - sumX * sumY) / (n * sumXX - sumX * sumX);
  50: const intercept = (sumY - slope * sumX) / n;
  ...
  58: const emissions = Number((slope * year + intercept).toFixed(2));
  59: forecast.push({ year, forecast: Math.max(0, emissions) });
  ```
- **Explanation:**
  If the dataset has 2 or more points with identical years (e.g. multiple entries for the same reporting year, or deduplicated data points with identical X values), `n * sumXX - sumX * sumX === 0`.
  Dividing by zero makes `slope` equal `NaN` or `Infinity`.
  Then `intercept` becomes `NaN`.
  Then `emissions` becomes `NaN`. `Math.max(0, NaN)` returns `NaN`.
  `forecast.push({ year, forecast: NaN })` inserts `NaN` values into `trendData`.
  Passing `NaN` to `LineChartWrapper` (Recharts `ResponsiveContainer`) causes invalid SVG coordinate calculations (`d="M...NaN...NaN"`), leading to console error spam and a broken line chart.
- **Corrected Code:**
  ```javascript
  const calculateForecast = (data) => {
    if (!data || data.length < 2) return [];

    const n = data.length;
    let sumX = 0,
      sumY = 0,
      sumXY = 0,
      sumXX = 0;

    data.forEach((p) => {
      sumX += p.year;
      sumY += p.emissions;
      sumXY += p.year * p.emissions;
      sumXX += p.year * p.year;
    });

    const denominator = n * sumXX - sumX * sumX;
    if (denominator === 0 || !isFinite(denominator)) return [];

    const slope = (n * sumXY - sumX * sumY) / denominator;
    const intercept = (sumY - slope * sumX) / n;

    if (!isFinite(slope) || !isFinite(intercept)) return [];

    const lastYear = data[data.length - 1].year;
    const forecast = [];

    for (let i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
      const year = lastYear + i;
      const val = slope * year + intercept;
      if (isFinite(val)) {
        forecast.push({ year, forecast: Math.max(0, Number(val.toFixed(2))) });
      }
    }
    return forecast;
  };
  ```

